index 2ff3ca1968d6cff1b823e813f022a397f405e0fa..e7c5db70e2058dacda4b0a0c8cf20c3eeba66090 100644
--- a/Changelog.rst
+++ b/Changelog.rst
@@ -593,6 +593,31 @@ Configuration:
 Contributed by `@MarcBresson <https://github.com/MarcBresson>`_ in
 `#9228 <https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/9228>`_.
 
+New ``database_engine_callback`` option for the database backend. When set,
+this callable is invoked with the SQLAlchemy engine immediately after it is
+created, allowing custom engine configuration such as registering
+connection-level event listeners or pragmas. The callback may be a Python
+callable or a dotted import path string, and can also be passed as the
+``engine_callback`` constructor keyword argument, which takes precedence over
+the configuration setting. A non-callable value raises
+:exc:`~@ImproperlyConfigured`.
+
+See :ref:`conf-database-result-backend` for complete documentation.
+
+Configuration:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from sqlalchemy import event
+
+    def register_do_connect(engine):
+        @event.listens_for(engine, 'do_connect')
+        def on_connect(dialect, conn_rec, cargs, cparams):
+            cparams['application_name'] = 'celery'
+
+    app.conf.result_backend = 'db+sqlite:///results.db'
+    app.conf.database_engine_callback = register_do_connect
+
 What's Changed
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
